### Private documents

`docs/planning/`, `docs/iterations/` and `docs/architecture/design/` are in `.gitignore`, so
they can hold information that shouldn't be public, and nothing in them reaches GitHub. They
exist only on this machine, which has these consequences:

- Don't run `git clean -x` or `git clean -X`, because those delete ignored files.
- A fresh clone or a git worktree doesn't have them. Give an agent working in one what it
  needs in its prompt.
- Search tools such as `rg` skip ignored files, so read these by path, or use
  `rg --no-ignore docs/`.
- Public text doesn't link to them or quote them: the README, the website, issue forms, commit
  messages and pull requests.

## Building, testing and checks

`scripts/check.sh` runs every check that must pass before a piece of work is done:
formatting, linting, complexity, tests, and the licenses of dependencies. CI runs the same
script on every push and pull request.
<!-- if RUST -->

### Rust

```sh
cargo build
cargo test
cargo fmt --check
cargo clippy --all-targets -- -D warnings
cargo clippy --all-targets -- -W clippy::cognitive_complexity -W clippy::too_many_lines
cargo deny check licenses
```

`rust-toolchain.toml` pins the toolchain.
<!-- end RUST -->
<!-- if JAVA -->

### Java

```sh
./mvnw verify                                  # tests, formatting, PMD and license checks
./mvnw spotless:apply                          # format the code
./mvnw com.mycila:license-maven-plugin:format  # add missing license headers
```

`pom.xml` sets the Java version: the newest stable JDK when the project was set up, without
preview features. `.sdkmanrc`, if the project has one, pins the JDK (`sdk env install`).
<!-- end JAVA -->
<!-- if HASKELL -->

### Haskell

```sh
cabal build all
cabal test all
ormolu --no-cabal --mode inplace $(find app src test -name '*.hs')
```

`cabal.project` pins GHC with `with-compiler`: the newest stable release when the project
was set up. `cabal.project.freeze` pins the dependencies (`cabal freeze`).
<!-- end HASKELL -->
<!-- if FRONTEND -->

### Frontend

```sh
npm --prefix {{FRONTEND_DIR}} install
npm --prefix {{FRONTEND_DIR}} run dev
npm --prefix {{FRONTEND_DIR}} run build
(cd {{FRONTEND_DIR}} && npx oxfmt)                 # format the code
```

`.nvmrc` and `engines` in `package.json` pin Node. `scripts/check.sh` also runs Oxfmt,
Oxlint, the type check, Vitest, Playwright and `licensee`. Browser tests go in `e2e/`, and
unit tests next to the code in `src/`.
<!-- if ASTRO -->
`tsc --noEmit --runExternalCode` checks `.astro` files through
`@astrojs/ts-content-mapper`. `astro check` isn't used, because it refuses TypeScript 7.
<!-- end ASTRO -->
<!-- end FRONTEND -->
